    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-13136",
      "problem": "Write the following statement using element notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $1$ and $2$ are elements of a set $S,$ but $3,$ $4,$ and $5$ are not.",
      "worked_solution": "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a \\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a \\notin S.$\n\n- Since $1$ and $2$ are elements of $S,$ we write $1,2 \\in S.$\n\n- Since $3,$ $4,$ and $5$ are *not* elements of $S,$ we write $3,4,5 \\notin S.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$$\n1,2 \\in S\\quad \\textrm{and}\\quad 3,4,5 \\notin S\n$$",
